# API collection

This application owns its recorded API evidence and generated references. The pinned apimesh toolchain lives at `__APIMESH_VENDOR__/`.

## Setup and import

Requires Git, Node.js 20+ and npm. After cloning with submodules:

```sh
git submodule update --init --recursive
npm run setup
```

Set the display name, observed origins and credential field names in `collection.json`. Keep glossary terms evidence-based. Put private HAR recordings in ignored `sources/`, then run:

```sh
npm run extract
```

This processes every direct `.har` file in `sources/` as one sorted batch. To select a batch explicitly, use `npm run extract -- "sources/capture.har"`. Inputs are unchanged; masked drafts go to `.raw/`. Inspect application-specific privacy needs before publishing canonical examples. Custom sanitization belongs in this application; the default masker does not guarantee coverage of every private field or embedded payload.

Follow `__APIMESH_VENDOR__/workflow/skills/classify/SKILL.md` to maintain canonical definitions and examples in `apis/`. Classification requires interpretation; it is not a CLI subcommand. Then run:

```sh
npm run verify
```

Verification validates strictly, renders twice, compares all output paths and bytes, and checks local replay. It writes actual results to `.reports/verify.json`. No recordings means replay fails; a freshly initialized repository has not completed an import. After an import, record source scope, unresolved frames and actual check results in your review handoff; no completed import report is supplied by initialization.

## Outputs and review

- Documentation: `dist/docs/summary.md`
- Agent references: `dist/agent/index.json`
- Postman: `dist/postman/endpoints.postman_collection.json` and `replay.postman_environment.json`
- Interactive replay: `npm run serve`
- Other commands: `npm run apic -- --help`

Commit reviewed metadata, canonical data, generated root `dist/`, setup files and the vendor pin. Originals in `sources/`, drafts and reports are ignored by default. CI runs `npm run verify -- --committed`; it requires a commit and clean generated output before and after rendering, including staged and untracked changes. It does not need private HAR files and does not call live APIs.

To upgrade apimesh, select a reviewed vendor commit, run `npm run setup` and `npm run verify`, then review and commit the pin and regenerated artifacts together. Repeating `apic init` only creates missing files; reconcile existing setup files with upstream templates explicitly.
